# `lab/` — Protocols and bench-record boundary

## Authority

The root [`README.md`](../README.md) contract defines placement. Bench facts are
human-owned; local [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) prohibits invention.

## Use this directory for

- Reusable protocols and SOPs, preferably as diffable text plus any necessary
  source attachment.
- Stable pointers connecting repository samples/analyses to the configured
  bench-record authority.
- {% if bench_record_authority == "repository" %}Human-created executed records
  under [`records/`](records/README.md).{% else %}Context needed to find the
  authoritative ELN record, without copying its executed facts into a competing
  repository log.{% endif %}

Machine-readable `sample_id → condition → file` mappings belong in `metadata/`,
not here. Raw measurements belong in `data/raw/`. Questions, claims, and
research decisions belong {% if use_lab_tracker %}in Lab Tracker{% else %}in the
documented repository decision fallback{% endif %}, not in a protocol.

## Configured bench-record authority

{% if bench_record_authority == "eln" -%}
**Electronic lab notebook (ELN).** Executed protocol facts, observations,
reagent lots, sample handling, dates, and deviations remain in the ELN.
{% if bench_record_location %}
Configured location: `{{ bench_record_location }}`.
{% else %}
**Location: UNCONFIGURED.** Do not guess an ELN notebook, workspace, project, or
entry. Ask the user before relying on or recording bench facts.
{% endif %}

This repository may keep a stable pointer and reusable protocol source, not a
second hand-maintained transcription of the executed record.
{% else -%}
**Repository records.** Human-created executed facts live only under
`lab/records/`. Use one dated record per execution and link its stable sample IDs
to validated `metadata/` rows. Do not use ordinary `notes/` or protocol source as
an execution log.
{% endif -%}
